PART 2: UNDERSTANDING VS CODE EXTENSIONS

================================================================================

What is an Extension?

A VS Code extension is a plugin that adds or enhances functionality in VS Code.

Extensions can be:

Created by Microsoft or third-party developers.
Free or paid.
Installed when required.
Enabled or disabled.
Uninstalled when no longer needed.
Types of Extensions
Extension Type       | Purpose
---------------------|---------------------------------------------
Productivity         | Speed up coding and automate tasks
Language             | Language support, syntax, completion, etc.
Theme                | Change colors/appearance
Debugging/Tooling    | Help inspect, test and debug applications


================================================================================

PART 3: HOW TO INSTALL EXTENSIONS

================================================================================

Method 1: Extensions Marketplace
Step | Action
-----|-----------------------------------------------------------
1    | Open VS Code
2    | Open Extensions from the Activity Bar
3    | Windows/Linux shortcut: Ctrl+Shift+X
4    | macOS shortcut: Cmd+Shift+X
5    | Search for the extension
6    | Select the required extension
7    | Click "Install"
8    | Wait for installation to complete

Example: ES7+ React/Redux/React-Native Snippets
Step | Action
-----|------------------------------------------------------
1    | Open Extensions
2    | Search "ES7+ React/Redux/React-Native snippets"
3    | Select the extension
4    | Click Install
5    | Extension becomes available


