Extension 2: Prettier - Code Formatter

================================================================================

Purpose

Prettier formats source code consistently.

It can help with:

Indentation
Spacing
Line formatting
Consistent code style
Readability
Basic Usage
Step | Action
-----|----------------------------------------------
1    | Install Prettier
2    | Open a source file
3    | Right-click in editor
4    | Select "Format Document"


Common formatting shortcut from the lesson:

Windows/Linux | Shift+Alt+F
macOS         | Shift+Option+F

Before Formatting
import React,{useState} from 'react'
export default function App(){
const[count,setCount]=useState(0)
return(
<div>
<h1>Count: {count}</h1>
<button onClick={()=>setCount(count+1)}>Increment</button>
</div>
)
}

After Formatting
import React, { useState } from "react";

export default function App() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Count: {count}</h1>
      <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>
        Increment
      </button>
    </div>
  );
}

Benefits
Before Prettier       | After Formatting
----------------------|----------------------------------
Inconsistent spacing  | Consistent spacing
Poor indentation      | Proper indentation
Harder to scan        | Easier to read
Manual formatting     | Formatter handles formatting


