PART 9: BEST PRACTICES

================================================================================

Best Practice 1: Install Only What You Need
Avoid installing extensions just because they are available.
Install tools relevant to your projects.
Disable/remove redundant extensions.
Keep your editor setup manageable.
Best Practice 2: Keep Extensions Updated
Review available updates.
Apply appropriate updates.
Benefit from fixes and improvements.
Best Practice 3: Configure Extensions Properly
Customize settings for project requirements.
Follow team formatting/linting standards.
Document important configurations.
Share project configuration where appropriate.
Best Practice 4: Learn Extension Features

Use useful features such as:

Keyboard shortcuts.
Code completion.
Snippets.
Formatters.
Quick fixes.
API-testing tools.
Best Practice 5: Review Extensions Regularly
Review
  ↓
Still Needed?
  ↓
YES → Keep/Update

NO
  ↓
Disable or Uninstall


